# DIEP MQTT access control.
# Topic layout: diep/<domain>/<deviceId>            (telemetry, 3 levels)
#               diep/<domain>/<deviceId>/cmd        (command,   4 levels)
#               diep/<domain>/<deviceId>/ack        (ack,       4 levels)

# Node-RED is the trusted controller: it issues commands, and reads telemetry + acks.
user diep-nodered
topic read diep/+/+
topic read diep/+/+/ack
topic write diep/+/+/cmd

# Devices (simulators): publish telemetry + acks, receive commands.
# Crucially NOT granted write on .../cmd — a device cannot spoof commands.
user diep-device
topic read diep/+/+/cmd
topic write diep/+/+/ack
topic write diep/+/+

# Phase 9J-S4 — per-device mTLS identities (8883). The cert CN becomes the username
# (use_identity_as_username), and each device is scoped to ITS OWN topics only — a
# compromised device cannot read or write another device's data (vs the broad shared
# 'diep-device' identity above). One block per migrated device.
user INV001
topic write diep/solar/INV001
topic read diep/solar/INV001/cmd
topic write diep/solar/INV001/ack

user METER001
topic write diep/smartmeter/METER001
topic read diep/smartmeter/METER001/cmd
topic write diep/smartmeter/METER001/ack

user BAT001
topic write diep/battery/BAT001
topic read diep/battery/BAT001/cmd
topic write diep/battery/BAT001/ack

user MG001
topic write diep/microgrid/MG001
topic read diep/microgrid/MG001/cmd
topic write diep/microgrid/MG001/ack

user EV001
topic write diep/charger/EV001
topic read diep/charger/EV001/cmd
topic write diep/charger/EV001/ack

# OCPP CSMS hosts many chargers, so it gets charger-domain scope (not a single device).
user csms
topic write diep/charger/+
topic read diep/charger/+/cmd
topic write diep/charger/+/ack

# Platform infra services (mTLS). Broad scope: ingestor reads all telemetry;
# dispatcher reads acks + issues commands. These replace the shared diep-nodered identity.
user ingestor
topic read diep/+/+

user dispatcher
topic read diep/+/+/ack
topic write diep/+/+/cmd
